1
00:01:03,394 --> 00:01:09,558
Morning, Grandpa.

2
00:01:09,558 --> 00:02:05,074
Is something the matter, Grandpa?

3
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:13,030
The editorial in this paper has my friend Nat Baker real upset.

4
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:15,976
Ah! I'll read it to you.

5
00:02:15,976 --> 00:02:19,043
"The old library building on Chestnut Street, “Chestnut

6
00:02:19,043 --> 00:02:22,524
which has been vacant for over a year now,

7
00:02:22,524 --> 00:02:25,496
was supposed to be made into a community center

8
00:02:25,496 --> 00:02:27,120
to serve the senior citizens

9
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,744
as well as the younger people of Riverdale.

10
00:02:29,744 --> 00:02:31,876
Due to lack of funds

11
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,854
for the repainting of the interior of the building

12
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,654
and for the furniture needed,

13
00:02:36,654 --> 00:02:39,066
the plans for the community center

14
00:02:39,066 --> 00:02:40,810
have been postponed indefinitely."

15
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:45,217
He's coming over to talk about it.

16
00:02:45,217 --> 00:02:48,195
Is it that serious a problem, Grandpa?

17
00:02:48,195 --> 00:02:49,744
It is.

18
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:54,402
Nat's not as lucky as I am, Robbie. Nat

19
00:02:54,402 --> 00:02:57,273
He doesn't have any family with him.

20
00:02:57,273 --> 00:02:59,633
He lives alone

21
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:01,303
and depends on places like a community center

22
00:03:01,303 --> 00:03:05,920
to be with people--people his own age.

23
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:10,045
But there's the old community center on Elm Street.

24
00:03:10,045 --> 00:03:10,989
It's small,

25
00:03:10,989 --> 00:03:17,545
and the problem is that it's set up primarily for kids to play.

26
00:03:17,545 --> 00:03:22,501
Ping-Pong tables, soda machines, and lots of music.

27
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:27,159
It's too noisy for some older people like Nat.

28
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:28,457
I never realized that.

29
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:34,413
It's hard for some older people to take all that noise.

30
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:37,391
That's why the new community center is a good idea.

31
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:38,942
Part of the building for older people,

32
00:03:38,942 --> 00:03:41,169
part of the building for younger people.

33
00:03:41,169 --> 00:03:43,347
I see what you mean.

34
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:47,413
That must be Nat.

35
00:03:47,413 --> 00:03:48,862
It could be Alexandra.

36
00:03:48,862 --> 00:03:58,237
She's coming over this morning to help me with my math.

37
00:03:58,237 --> 00:03:58,967
Hi, Robbie.

38
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:04,193
Hi, Alexandra. Come on in.

39
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:06,593
Do you want something cold to drink?

40
00:04:06,593 --> 00:04:08,851
I'd love some cola, please.

41
00:04:08,851 --> 00:04:10,149
Cola coming up.

42
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:15,567
I really appreciate you coming over to help me with my math.

43
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:16,534
My final exam is next Tuesday.

44
00:04:16,534 --> 00:04:19,759
You're so good in all your other subjects.

45
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,110
I just can't understand

46
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:23,727
why you have so many problems with math.

47
00:04:23,727 --> 00:04:24,560
Hi, Alexandra.

48
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,371
Hi, Mr. Stewart.

49
00:04:26,371 --> 00:04:30,994
I thought that was Nat Baker who rang the front doorbell.

50
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:32,744
Don't let me interrupt you.

51
00:04:32,744 --> 00:04:33,972
No problem, Grandpa.

52
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:35,245
We're just having some cola

53
00:04:35,245 --> 00:04:37,950
before getting to the tough stuff--math.

54
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:42,899
He'll do anything to avoid getting down to math lessons,

55
00:04:42,899 --> 00:04:43,402
Mr. Stewart. Stewart

56
00:04:43,402 --> 00:04:46,484
I was the same way.

57
00:04:46,484 --> 00:04:47,684
Really, Grandpa?

58
00:04:47,684 --> 00:04:50,350
Really. I didn't like math.

59
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:54,000
I wasn't good at it, and I didn't like studying it.

60
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,080
But you had to be good at math.

61
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,796
You graduated from engineering school.

62
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:00,774
I was. But not in high school.

63
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:03,752
For some reason, I couldn't get a handle on it.

64
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:07,930
Then, in college, I became good at it.

65
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:10,255
Then there's hope for Robbie.

66
00:05:10,255 --> 00:05:11,513
I can't wait.

67
00:05:11,513 --> 00:05:15,791
You think I can just skip it now and get to it at college?

68
00:05:15,791 --> 00:05:17,331
You'll never get to college to find out, Robbie,

69
00:05:17,331 --> 00:05:19,362
if you skip it now.

70
00:05:19,362 --> 00:05:23,060
That must be Nat.

71
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:36,509
Sit down, Robbie. Let's get to work.

72
00:05:36,509 --> 00:05:40,447
I'd like you to meet my friend Nat Baker.

73
00:05:40,447 --> 00:05:44,412
This is Alexandra Pappas, and this is my grandson Robbie,

74
00:05:44,412 --> 00:05:47,083
whom I think you've met once or twice before.

75
00:05:47,083 --> 00:05:48,421
Nice to meet you, Mr. Baker.

76
00:05:48,421 --> 00:05:51,399
Hi, Mr. Baker. We met before.

77
00:05:51,399 --> 00:05:51,828
Where?

78
00:05:51,828 --> 00:05:54,377
In town. At the hardware store.

79
00:05:54,377 --> 00:05:59,355
I remember now. Right. Hi.

80
00:05:59,355 --> 00:06:01,000
Hello, Alexandra.

81
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,064
Don't let us keep you from your math tutoring, Robbie.

82
00:06:04,064 --> 00:06:06,289
I know you want to get to it.

83
00:06:06,289 --> 00:06:08,289
Stay ... stay.

84
00:06:08,289 --> 00:06:12,245
I told you. He'll use any excuse to avoid math.

85
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:15,863
Did you read the story in the paper, Malcolm?

86
00:06:15,863 --> 00:06:16,503
I did.

87
00:06:16,503 --> 00:07:02,870
It's a serious matter for a lot of us.

88
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:04,070
A serious matter.

89
00:07:04,070 --> 00:07:22,881
It is. Come on out to the patio.

90
00:07:22,881 --> 00:08:13,196
We'll talk about it out there.

91
00:08:13,196 --> 00:08:26,253
Thanks. Nice to meet you ... again.

92
00:08:26,253 --> 00:08:29,231
What's the problem?

93
00:08:29,231 --> 00:08:32,231
Come on! You'll hear about it.
